{{also|fáce|facé|Face}}

==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|face}}, from {{der|en|fro|face}}, from {{der|en|LL.|facia}}, from {{der|en|la|faciēs||form, appearance}}. {{doublet|en|facies}}. Displaced native {{noncog|enm|onlete||face, countenance, appearance}}, {{m|enm|anleth||face}}, from {{noncog|ang|anwlite}}, {{m|ang|andwlita}}, compare {{noncog|de|Antlitz}}; {{noncog|ang|ansīen||face}}, {{noncog|enm|neb||face, nose}} (from {{noncog|ang|nebb}}), {{noncog|enm|leer|ler, leor, leer|face, cheek, countenance}} (from {{noncog|ang|hlēor}}), and non-native {{noncog|enm|vis||face, appearance, look}} (from {{noncog|fro|vis}}) and {{noncog|enm|chere|t=face}} from {{noncog|fro|chere}}.

